import{_ as i,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 932 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 31 | The Charter's Supreme Effect","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 932 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 31 | The Charter's Supreme Effect","no":932,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 31","Supreme Effect","Constitutionality Review","Constitutional Litigation"],"related":["03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","48-Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism","49-Governance Framework and Power Checks"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0932_模块5-第三十一条-宪章最高效力.md","filePath":"en/0932_模块5-第三十一条-宪章最高效力.md"}`),o={name:"en/0932_模块5-第三十一条-宪章最高效力.md"};function r(s,e,l,h,c,u){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-932-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-31-the-charter-s-supreme-effect" tabindex="-1">Entry 932 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 31 | The Charter&#39;s Supreme Effect <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-932-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-31-the-charter-s-supreme-effect" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 932 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 31 | The Charter&#39;s Supreme Effect&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 03, 48, 49</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-above-everything-stands-only-the-charter-itself" tabindex="-1">Introduction: above everything stands only the charter itself <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-above-everything-stands-only-the-charter-itself" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: above everything stands only the charter itself&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 30 governs &quot;how the charter is amended&quot;; Article 31 governs &quot;how high the charter stands.&quot; It stipulates: the charter is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s supreme law, with effect higher than all laws, all institutions, all strong ones, and all conventions. Any norm conflicting with the charter is void ab initio. This is no slogan — it is paired with constitutionality review and constitutional litigation, turning &quot;supreme effect&quot; from a paper title into enforceable reality.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Symbiotic Civilization Charter (Document 03)&#39;s constitutionality-review system, the Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism (Document 48), and the Governance Framework and Power Checks (Document 49). Its jurisprudence is the law-first axiom: the charter itself is the law&#39;s total expression among beings. No institution and no strong one may place himself outside the charter — the Anchor Council may not ride above it, the Symbiotic Executive Committee may not bypass it, plane-sovereign strong ones may not be exempt. Supreme effect means: in Myriad-Rank republicanism, the only highest is not some person, but the laws commonly established.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-three-layers-of-supreme-effect-guarantee" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Three Layers of Supreme-Effect Guarantee <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-three-layers-of-supreme-effect-guarantee" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Three Layers of Supreme-Effect Guarantee&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 31 concretizes supreme effect:</p><ol><li><strong>Conflict void</strong>: all local regulations, sect rules, clan customs, cross-plane conventions conflicting with the charter are void ab initio;</li><li><strong>Constitutional review</strong>: all laws and policies, before taking effect, must pass the Anchor Court&#39;s constitutionality review;</li><li><strong>Constitutional litigation</strong>: any being who believes a public-power act is unconstitutional may directly file constitutional litigation with the Anchor Court, without level-by-level approval.</li></ol><p>Three layers of guarantee make the charter&#39;s supreme effect directly invocable by ordinary beings.</p><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all subjects in Heng Yuan Zhou, including the tripartite institutions, all clans, all planes, and all individuals and strong ones. This article especially makes clear: no institution or individual stands &quot;above the charter&quot; — even Lin Hao who pioneered a route, even Transcended Ones who wield hyper-multiverse power, are equally bound by the charter. Planet consciousness and accepted multiverse-residual individuals likewise have the right to file constitutional litigation.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Enacting or applying unconstitutional norms, refusing constitutionality review, suppressing constitutional litigation, or declaring with institutional authority &quot;the charter does not bind me,&quot; all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: unconstitutional norms are immediately void, relevant acts are revoked; those using power to override law or placing themselves outside the charter have their power qualifications suspended, and are pursued heavily as undermining the fundamental law.</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by the constitutionality-review and litigation system within Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: all higher norms are automatically compared against the charter, and conflicts are blocked; the constitutional-litigation channel is open to all beings, and handling results are network-wide publicized; the Anchor Court independently exercises charter-interpretation power, free from any administrative interference.</p><h2 id="vi-a-litigation-the-weak-won" tabindex="-1">VI. A Litigation the Weak Won <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-a-litigation-the-weak-won" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. A Litigation the Weak Won&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 31&#39;s most powerful moment is a litigation the weak won. An ordinary cultivator from a marginal plane, believing some public policy discriminates against his group, directly files constitutional litigation with the Anchor Court. Not because of his low realm, not because he faces a high-and-mighty institution, the suit is accepted, and finally the policy is ruled unconstitutional and void. This judgment tells Myriad Ranks: in Heng Yuan Zhou, the charter is not wall decoration for the strong, but a weapon every weak person may use against the strong. When the weakest party may also use the supreme law to win over the strongest party, law-supremacy truly turns from slogan into reality.</p><h2 id="vii-axiom-6-s-projection-in-supreme-effect" tabindex="-1">VII. Axiom 6&#39;s Projection in Supreme Effect <a class="header-anchor" href="#vii-axiom-6-s-projection-in-supreme-effect" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VII. Axiom 6&#39;s Projection in Supreme Effect&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The universal equal infinite law grants every being a supreme-law weapon against discrimination: when any institution or any strong one tries to deny some individual&#39;s inherent basic infinite power, that individual may directly file constitutional litigation under the charter&#39;s supreme effect. Supreme effect thus belongs not only to grand clauses, but ultimately lands on the most concrete individual — no matter how easygoing, how ordinary, his innate share of basic infinity is guarded by the entire charter&#39;s supreme effect.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: all subjects obey the same supreme law, avoiding system internal friction from normative conflict</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: supreme effect equals declaring &quot;no one may stand above the anti-predation axiom&quot;</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in Tang-Luo-type systems the strong speak the law into being and are themselves the law; in Heng Yuan Zhou everyone is bound by the charter, including the strongest</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: constitutional-litigation right belongs to all; the weak may also use the charter against the strong</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: supreme effect covers every newly incorporated plane and civilization, without exception</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The charter&#39;s supreme effect is the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s rule of law apex. When Myriad Ranks confirm — the only highest is the common law, not any single strongest individual — this civilization truly escapes the cycle of &quot;rule by man.&quot; Law supreme, and Myriad-Rank republicanism is firm through the ages.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">Entry 03 · Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/48-司法体系与裁决机制.html">Entry 48 · Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">Entry 49 · Governance Framework and Power Checks</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/931_模块5-第三十条-宪章修订程序.html">Entry 931 · Article 30 Charter-Amendment Procedure</a></li></ul>',28)])])}const p=i(o,[["render",r]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
